      *> DESIGN EXAMPLE - NOT COMPILED OR PRODUCTION READY.
      *> Project policy pseudocode, not a CICS/DFSMStvs implementation.
      *> Mapping: W001..W005; CAP-001/CAP-008/CAP-009/CAP-026.
      *> Tests: AT-001, AT-007..AT-009, AT-022..AT-024.

       EVALUATE-PUBLICATION-BOUNDARY.
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN WRITER-UNMAPPED
                   PERFORM BLOCK-AFFECTED-ENTITY
               WHEN BATCH-WRITES-THROUGH-CICS
                   PERFORM REQUIRE-PROVEN-CICS-UOW-OUTCOME
               WHEN DIRECT-TVS-RRS-PATH-QUALIFIED
                   PERFORM REQUIRE-PROVEN-UOR-OUTCOME
               WHEN DIRECT-NONRECOVERABLE-BATCH
                   PERFORM REQUIRE-APPROVED-EXTERNAL-BOUNDARY
                   IF NOT BOUNDARY-PROVEN
                       PERFORM PERSIST-HELD-AND-ALERT
                   END-IF
               WHEN OTHER
                   PERFORM BLOCK-AFFECTED-ENTITY
           END-EVALUATE.

      *> This routine returns evidence/eligibility to the StateStore;
      *> it never publishes nor advances resume by itself.
      *> Job RC=0, EOF, CLOSE or an elapsed timeout is NOT commit proof.
      *> CICS replication logging does not automatically cover direct
      *> batch writes. CICS VR and DFSMStvs/RRS have different conditions.
      *> RLS alone is not transaction recovery.
      *> A validated batch window may have greater latency than online.
      *> An unsupported writer blocks the entity, not just that writer.
